# The app menu's "Modern controls" (wish of a user, 12.11.2026, Controls page): the left stick moves Leon in the
# direction it points, as the camera sees it, instead of the original's tank controls. Off (the default): as the game.
# player.cpp re4ModernPrepare runs before the movement routine (pl_R0_Move; only the free-moving routines: idle,
# walk, back step, run, turn): Leon turns toward the stick (at most 0.25 rad a frame) and the routine is told "up"
# (Key bit 1) only, with the back / left / right bits off (restored afterwards), so walk and run start and stop as
# always. The digital pad does the same. The shoulder camera follows Leon's yaw, so a camera-relative stick would
# circle: while Leon walks and stands the camera keeps a yaw of its own (g_re4_modern_cam_yaw, turned by the right
# stick; cam_qfps.cpp calcBaseMatrix builds its base matrix from it), otherwise the yaw follows Leon's. With the
# aim key held Leon first turns to where the camera looks, then the game's aim routine runs unchanged.
# Not covered: ladders, crouching, boats, pushing and the knife keep the original keys; the back step and the
# B+down quick turn are off while the switch is on (the stick turns him around instead).
